mechanism:
getRegForInlineAsmConstraint maps each constraint letter to a FIXED register class with NO regard for the operand MVT:
  case 'r': case 'f': return {0U, &NVPTX::B32RegClass};   // always 32-bit
  case 'l': case 'N': case 'd': return {0U, &NVPTX::B64RegClass};
  case 'c': case 'h': return {0U, &NVPTX::B16RegClass};
  case 'b': return {0U, &NVPTX::B1RegClass};
Unlike x86/AArch64 (which pick the class matching VT), NVPTX hardcodes the class. The generic glue in SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp GetRegistersForValue (~10073-10122) computes RegVT = legalclasstypes_begin(RC) (e.g. i32 for B32) and only repairs a constraint/regclass size mismatch in two cases: (a) equal sizes -> bitcast, (b) FP operand into an integer regclass -> int bitcast. When the operand is a *wider integer* (or a wider value that isn't FP-into-int) than RegVT, NEITHER repair fires, and the value is placed in RegsForValue(Regs, RegVT=i32, ValueVT=i64). The CopyToReg therefore truncates the i64/f64 to 32 bits before the asm and any-extends afterward. The high 32 bits are unconditionally discarded.

